WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.800
It's new, it's different, it's all alive. See the fabulous Little Egypt, who once danced for the Queen of England.

00:05.800 --> 00:11.100
Little Egypt, the shimmy dancer. Now with no confidence, folks, for those of you who've never seen the female figure,

00:11.100 --> 00:16.800
in delicious movement from head to toe. You can see it here for only 25 cents, one quarter of a dollar.

00:24.800 --> 00:27.800
Oh, ain't this the beatin'est dead gun thing you ever seen?

00:27.800 --> 00:31.600
Virginia City's really come of age, now that the carnival circuit has hit it.

00:33.600 --> 00:36.800
Oh, I can't stand it, look at me. Supposedly, we're the men.

00:36.800 --> 00:38.600
Oh, you're the men?

00:41.800 --> 00:43.600
You don't look very scared, Jennifer.

00:43.600 --> 00:45.100
What's there to be scared of?

00:45.100 --> 00:58.100
Give anything in the world to change places for that girl up there.

00:58.100 --> 01:02.100
Well, Adam, I guess you and I better get on our way. We've been here longer than we planned.

01:02.100 --> 01:09.100
Harriet, Jennifer, good night. Joe, you promised Mr. Beale faithfully you'd get the girl some by 10 o'clock tonight.

01:09.100 --> 01:10.100
Right.

01:10.100 --> 01:14.100
Mr. Cartwright, please. Do you have to remind me?

01:14.100 --> 01:16.100
Don't worry, Pa, I'll keep an eye on him.

01:16.100 --> 01:18.100
Good. Sure, Pa, but who's gonna keep an eye on him?

01:18.100 --> 01:20.100
...25 cents, a quarter of a dollar...

01:20.100 --> 01:22.100
...the most delectable package of...

01:22.100 --> 01:23.100
Isn't that right, Hoss?

01:23.100 --> 01:24.100
Hi.

01:24.100 --> 01:26.100
I mean, sir.

01:26.100 --> 01:29.100
He'll do fine, Pa, ask no more.

01:29.100 --> 01:48.100
You're going to see this charming little lady move every muscle in her body.

01:59.100 --> 02:22.100
Oh, good night, girls.

02:22.100 --> 02:24.100
Good night, Hoss.

02:24.100 --> 02:25.100
Joe, good night, Pa.

02:25.100 --> 02:26.100
Good night.

02:26.100 --> 02:31.100
Hey.

02:31.100 --> 02:34.100
It's just the beat-inest death-burn thing you've ever seen, Joe.

02:34.100 --> 02:37.100
No, you're just not kidding.

02:37.100 --> 02:39.100
Looking at anything special, Garner?

02:39.100 --> 02:41.100
That girl, the redhead.

02:41.100 --> 02:42.100
She looks familiar.

02:42.100 --> 02:44.100
Hey, you reckon what we ought to take in first?

02:44.100 --> 02:46.100
How about the mystic tent? I'd like to have my fortune told.

02:46.100 --> 02:47.100
All right.

02:47.100 --> 02:49.100
That's what I'd like to hear about. Wouldn't you, Harriet?

02:49.100 --> 02:52.100
Not if it's any bad news, I wouldn't.

02:52.100 --> 02:57.100
She's been plastered all over the front pages of the San Francisco paper for the past couple of months.

02:57.100 --> 03:00.100
That's Joshua Beale's daughter.

03:00.100 --> 03:01.100
Joshua Beale?

03:01.100 --> 03:02.100
Mm-hmm.

03:02.100 --> 03:04.100
The silver king.

03:04.100 --> 03:06.100
He's one of the richest men in the world.

03:06.100 --> 03:09.100
Stop dreaming, Garner.

03:09.100 --> 03:10.100
The big show begins.

03:10.100 --> 03:16.100
The most electrifying set-back ever to appear on the Midway West of the Mississippi.

03:16.100 --> 03:20.100
Just once in my life, I'd like to get my hands on some real money.

03:20.100 --> 03:25.100
What do you suppose Beale figures that daughter's worth to him?

03:25.100 --> 03:29.100
More money than we'll ever see, Garner.

03:41.100 --> 03:44.100
Hey, Hoss, you gonna let this guy read your future?

03:44.100 --> 03:46.100
I don't know. I might just take him on.

03:46.100 --> 03:51.100
Ever since that old Paiute squaw read my palm and told me I was gonna be taking that long trip,

03:51.100 --> 03:55.100
I've been plumb off my feed bag. I can't eat but five or six meals.

03:58.100 --> 03:59.100
Hey!

03:59.100 --> 04:07.100
Now, if one of you will give to my assistant some personal object.

04:11.100 --> 04:15.100
Don't be afraid, ladies and gentlemen. Nothing will happen to it.

04:15.100 --> 04:19.100
If you please, some personal object.

04:19.100 --> 04:26.100
Are you ready, Mr. Wizard? I am ready.

04:26.100 --> 04:29.100
Then can you tell me what I'm holding in my hand?

04:29.100 --> 04:35.100
I see a round object of precious metal.

04:35.100 --> 04:40.100
I hear a strange sound within the room.

04:40.100 --> 04:43.100
I hear a strange sound.

04:43.100 --> 04:50.100
I believe it is a gold pocket watch.

04:52.100 --> 04:54.100
Joe, how do you reckon he does that?

04:54.100 --> 04:55.100
He's a heck out of me.

04:55.100 --> 04:57.100
You think it's some sort of trick?

04:57.100 --> 04:58.100
Of course it's a trick.

04:58.100 --> 04:59.100
How do you know?

04:59.100 --> 05:00.100
Well, I just know.

05:00.100 --> 05:02.100
Silence!

05:02.100 --> 05:08.100
And now, I will bring to you the most important object of all time.

05:08.100 --> 05:20.100
Silence! And now, I will bring to you one of the most astounding disappearance acts in the annals of all magic.

05:20.100 --> 05:27.100
And tonight, just to prove to you that this is truly an outstanding and remarkable feat,

05:27.100 --> 05:33.100
instead of using my regular assistant, I shall ask one of you to assist me.

05:33.100 --> 05:38.100
Is there a young lady in the audience who would like to disappear for a few minutes?

05:38.100 --> 05:42.100
I assure you it's a thrill that you have never realized before.

05:42.100 --> 05:43.100
I'd like to try.

05:43.100 --> 05:44.100
Jennifer.

05:44.100 --> 05:46.100
I don't want your call set about leaving little Joe's sight.

05:46.100 --> 05:48.100
You didn't say anything about this.

05:48.100 --> 05:50.100
And besides, this will be fun.

05:50.100 --> 05:54.100
But if you disappear, that's going to be leaving his sight, ain't it?

05:54.100 --> 05:55.100
Jennifer, sit down.

05:55.100 --> 05:58.100
Everybody's looking at you.

05:58.100 --> 06:00.100
Joe, don't you think you ought to stop her?

06:00.100 --> 06:04.100
I'm not going to let her go ahead. It's just a trick.

06:04.100 --> 06:08.100
It seems a shame to make such a pretty young lady disappear.

06:08.100 --> 06:12.100
Don't worry, young man. I'll have her back to you soon enough.

06:15.100 --> 06:21.100
Now, you see, ladies and gentlemen, that this is an ordinary wardrobe top.

06:24.100 --> 06:25.100
Young lady.

06:25.100 --> 06:28.100
Young lady.

06:56.100 --> 06:57.100
Where am I?

06:58.100 --> 06:59.100
Backstage.

07:00.100 --> 07:02.100
And I open it.

07:06.100 --> 07:08.100
Why is she always doing things like that?

07:08.100 --> 07:11.100
Like the time she ran off to San Francisco.

07:11.100 --> 07:13.100
I kind of like it, Joe. She's got a lot of spunk.

07:13.100 --> 07:17.100
The young lady will reappear when the mystic spirits are willing.

07:17.100 --> 07:22.100
And now, ladies and gentlemen, while that beautiful young lady is out there floating around in space,

07:22.100 --> 07:27.100
I offer you for two bits a quarter pound of a dollar this elixir of life.

07:27.100 --> 07:30.100
You know, young ladies, since you were kind enough to join our act,

07:30.100 --> 07:32.100
I hope you'll be discreet enough to keep our secret.

07:32.100 --> 07:34.100
I'm Phil Reed, owner of the show.

07:34.100 --> 07:40.100
Oh, I won't tell. But I must say, I certainly expected much more than a back door in a trunk.

07:40.100 --> 07:43.100
Hmm. I guess our magic is pretty simple, huh?

07:43.100 --> 07:45.100
Is it?

07:45.100 --> 07:49.100
You know what? This is the most fascinating place I've ever seen.

07:49.100 --> 07:51.100
I, uh, I think you better get back in that trunk.

07:51.100 --> 07:54.100
It won't take long before he sells all the snake art.

07:54.100 --> 07:56.100
Even when you know the tricks.

07:56.100 --> 08:00.100
It's such a strange atmosphere. Such an air of excitement about it all.

08:01.100 --> 08:02.100
It's a living.

08:03.100 --> 08:06.100
Oh, I'm sure it's much more than that.

08:09.100 --> 08:10.100
Much more.

08:10.100 --> 08:13.100
Much more.

08:15.100 --> 08:17.100
I think you better get back to your friends, huh?

08:17.100 --> 08:21.100
Please, Mr. Reed. I can get away from my friends.

08:22.100 --> 08:26.100
Now look, if you're not in that box when he opens it, the whole act is gonna be ruined.

08:30.100 --> 08:33.100
Isn't there any way I can change your mind, Mr. Reed?

08:35.100 --> 08:39.100
Aren't you afraid of what could happen to you in a circus sideshow alone?

08:39.100 --> 08:41.100
Afraid?

08:42.100 --> 08:46.100
Mr. Reed, I'm not afraid of anything.

08:46.100 --> 08:48.100
I'll bet you're not.

08:48.100 --> 08:56.100
And now, ladies and gentlemen, I think that the beautiful young lady who has been so far away from us, they have returned.

08:56.100 --> 09:03.100
And now, ladies and gentlemen, I think that the beautiful young lady who has been so far away from us, they have returned.

09:03.100 --> 09:15.100
And now, ladies and gentlemen, I think that the beautiful young lady who has been so far away from us, they have returned.

09:30.100 --> 09:32.100
Hey, where'd you go off to?

09:32.100 --> 09:34.100
Far, far away.

09:34.100 --> 09:35.100
No, really.

09:35.100 --> 09:36.100
It's all the way behind that curtain over there.

09:36.100 --> 09:38.100
Well, Jennifer, aren't you gonna tell us about it?

09:38.100 --> 09:40.100
Maybe. Someday.

09:40.100 --> 09:43.100
And that's only the beginning, folks. Only the beginning.

09:43.100 --> 09:48.100
I want to call your attention to one of the most sensational acts ever presented west of the Mississippi.

09:48.100 --> 09:55.100
In just a few moments, directly next door, we're going to present the 350-pound strongman, Hercules.

09:55.100 --> 09:57.100
Just follow me right this way.

09:57.100 --> 10:00.100
The greatest act in the sky ever presented on our midway.

10:00.100 --> 10:06.100
Right this way, you'll love it. It's the most sensational, outstanding act in the sky.

10:06.100 --> 10:14.100
And now, ladies and gentlemen, Hercules is going to bend this solid one-inch iron bar like it was made out of this sawdust on the floor.

10:14.100 --> 10:16.100
Hercules?

10:25.100 --> 10:27.100
How about that, folks?

10:27.100 --> 10:29.100
Hey.

10:29.100 --> 10:34.100
Would you like to examine that bar, sir, to see that it's genuine?

10:34.100 --> 10:36.100
Thank you.

10:38.100 --> 10:40.100
Would you like to examine this, sir?

10:40.100 --> 10:42.100
Try that right in there, sir.

10:42.100 --> 10:47.100
Right in there, sir.

10:54.100 --> 10:56.100
Ladies and gentlemen, I...

10:56.100 --> 10:58.100
Smart aleckers.

10:59.100 --> 11:07.100
Ladies and gentlemen, if there's anybody in the audience who doubts the genuine strength of Hercules or thinks that this is some form of trickery,

11:07.100 --> 11:12.100
Hercules is now ready to match his strength against any two men in the audience.

11:12.100 --> 11:23.100
And furthermore, we're prepared to offer 50 bucks, $50, to any man or woman who can force Hercules across this white line within the time limit of one minute.

11:23.100 --> 11:25.100
Do we have any takers, huh?

11:25.100 --> 11:30.100
What about you two stalwart young gentlemen down there, huh, with the two beautiful young ladies, huh?

11:30.100 --> 11:31.100
Us?

11:31.100 --> 11:35.100
Yeah, you two. Come on up, boys, and show the girls how strong you are.

11:35.100 --> 11:39.100
Go on, little Joe. You're not afraid to at least try, are you?

11:39.100 --> 11:41.100
Why, he's bigger than anything.

11:41.100 --> 11:43.100
Would you like to try your luck?

11:43.100 --> 11:45.100
Come on, Os, I think we can take him.

11:45.100 --> 11:46.100
You're on?

11:46.100 --> 11:47.100
Let's go.

11:52.100 --> 11:58.100
All right, gentlemen, the time limit is one minute, remember, to pull Hercules across this white line.

11:58.100 --> 11:59.100
Are you ready?

11:59.100 --> 12:00.100
Go!

12:00.100 --> 12:06.100
And now there, ladies and gentlemen, is the greatest advertisement in the world for our elixir of life.

12:06.100 --> 12:11.100
Would you believe it, folks, at one time, this poor boy was only a 74-pound weakling.

12:11.100 --> 12:16.100
And after 90 days and 90 nights, Hercules taking this elixir of life.

12:16.100 --> 12:18.100
Today, look at the results.

12:18.100 --> 12:22.100
355 pounds of solid blubber, or muscle.

12:22.100 --> 12:24.100
There he is, folks, Hercules.

12:24.100 --> 12:27.100
One time, 74-pound weakling.

12:27.100 --> 12:30.100
Come on!

12:33.100 --> 12:37.100
Hey, hey, hey, hey, Hercules is the winner. Hercules is the winner now.

12:37.100 --> 12:39.100
Thank you very much, gentlemen.

12:39.100 --> 12:41.100
Thank you. Let's keep moving it along, folks.

12:41.100 --> 12:44.100
Keep it moving along. Some wonderful shows out on the midway.

12:44.100 --> 12:48.100
See the sword swallower and the fire eater who swallows hot food right out of the...

12:48.100 --> 12:50.100
Jennifer's gone. She's disappeared out of the tent.

12:50.100 --> 12:52.100
She's gone. Did you see her leave?

12:52.100 --> 12:54.100
I was watching the stage.

12:54.100 --> 12:56.100
Why is she always doing things like this?

12:56.100 --> 12:58.100
It's probably just her idea of some kind of a joke.

12:58.100 --> 13:00.100
We gotta find her.

13:00.100 --> 13:02.100
We're gonna find her.

13:02.100 --> 13:04.100
And when we find her, I'm gonna hog-tire for the rest of the evening.

13:04.100 --> 13:06.100
Come on. Come on, let's go.

13:06.100 --> 13:08.100
Let's find out where she could be.

13:14.100 --> 13:16.100
You didn't do so good tonight out there, Della.

13:16.100 --> 13:20.100
Don't start an argument with me, Phil. Not tonight. I'm tired.

13:20.100 --> 13:22.100
I'm talking about the good of the show.

13:22.100 --> 13:25.100
Those rubes pay their money to see you give a performance.

13:25.100 --> 13:28.100
How long do I have to keep on doing this?

13:28.100 --> 13:30.100
You told me a year ago we could get married.

13:30.100 --> 13:32.100
I could get out of the act and help you run the show.

13:32.100 --> 13:36.100
Next time you go on, you give them their money's worth.

13:46.100 --> 13:48.100
Another argument?

13:48.100 --> 13:50.100
Oh, no, not really.

13:50.100 --> 13:53.100
Just that I know him so well.

13:53.100 --> 13:56.100
He saw a pretty young girl out in the audience tonight.

13:56.100 --> 13:58.100
Captured his fancy.

13:58.100 --> 14:01.100
He looks at her, wanting her, and...

14:01.100 --> 14:03.100
then he looks at me.

14:05.100 --> 14:08.100
Why don't you let me be the mystic in the show, huh?

14:10.100 --> 14:12.100
I'll tell you what we'll do.

14:12.100 --> 14:14.100
As soon as Hercules finishes his act,

14:14.100 --> 14:17.100
the three of us will go out and have a cup of coffee together.

14:17.100 --> 14:23.100
I'll tell you fortune.

14:36.100 --> 14:39.100
Oh, Mr. Reed. I was looking for you.

14:39.100 --> 14:41.100
I can't say I'm not flattered.

14:41.100 --> 14:44.100
What are you doing wandering around out here alone?

14:44.100 --> 14:46.100
What do you propose to do about it?

14:46.100 --> 14:48.100
Send me back again?

14:48.100 --> 14:50.100
Is there any reason why I shouldn't?

14:50.100 --> 14:53.100
Just one, Mr. Reed. It wouldn't do any good.

14:53.100 --> 14:56.100
How does your father put up with you?

14:56.100 --> 14:59.100
Oh, Father. He just doesn't understand me.

14:59.100 --> 15:03.100
He doesn't realize I'm not as conservative as young ladies of his day.

15:04.100 --> 15:07.100
Why don't we go someplace where we can talk?

15:07.100 --> 15:09.100
I was hoping you'd say that.

15:09.100 --> 15:11.100
My wagon's right here.

15:11.100 --> 15:17.100
Let's go.

15:27.100 --> 15:30.100
Someday I'll kill him for what he does to her.

15:30.100 --> 15:32.100
Poor Hercules.

15:32.100 --> 15:36.100
Do you think that will make her love him?

15:36.100 --> 15:39.100
I had no idea a sideshow wagon would be like this.

15:39.100 --> 15:41.100
Not all of them are.

15:41.100 --> 15:44.100
But there has to be some compensation for owning the show.

15:44.100 --> 15:46.100
I'm sure there must be.

15:46.100 --> 15:48.100
What do you mean by that?

15:48.100 --> 15:52.100
Let's say compensation such as

15:52.100 --> 15:55.100
entertaining young ladies in your private quarters.

15:55.100 --> 15:58.100
Isn't that right, Mr. Reed?

15:58.100 --> 16:01.100
You're a very attractive young lady.

16:01.100 --> 16:04.100
Thank you. You're very kind.

16:04.100 --> 16:08.100
Thank you. You're a very handsome man.

16:10.100 --> 16:15.100
Now, Mr. Reed, I thought we came in here to talk.

16:15.100 --> 16:17.100
Can't you knock?

16:17.100 --> 16:19.100
I can if I want to.

16:19.100 --> 16:21.100
Hello, Miss Beale.

16:21.100 --> 16:23.100
I didn't tell you my name.

16:23.100 --> 16:25.100
Oh, I know your name.

16:25.100 --> 16:27.100
I know your father's name, too.

16:27.100 --> 16:31.100
Joshua Beale. The richest man on the Comstock.

16:31.100 --> 16:35.100
How much do you suppose you're worth to that father of yours, Miss Beale?

16:35.100 --> 16:37.100
Are you out of your mind, Gurner?

16:37.100 --> 16:40.100
I, Mr. Reed, or you, if you miss this chance.

16:40.100 --> 16:42.100
We can break camp tonight.

16:42.100 --> 16:45.100
By tomorrow morning, we can be over the mountain and well on our way to Placerville.

16:45.100 --> 16:48.100
All you have to do is write a note to Joshua Beale.

16:50.100 --> 16:52.100
One million dollars.

16:52.100 --> 16:56.100
That's all it'll cost him to get his pretty little girl back home.

16:56.100 --> 16:58.100
You'll never get away with this.

16:58.100 --> 17:00.100
With your help, I can, Reed.

17:00.100 --> 17:02.100
Listen, Reed, one million dollars.

17:02.100 --> 17:04.100
You know what that could mean?

17:04.100 --> 17:07.100
You always wanted to make some big money.

17:11.100 --> 17:13.100
Shut up! Don't scream, lady.

17:13.100 --> 17:15.100
This is a sharp knife.

17:19.100 --> 17:21.100
Where do you think you'd hide her?

17:21.100 --> 17:23.100
I thought you'd figure out a way.

17:23.100 --> 17:25.100
You ought to hold her like I'm doing.

17:25.100 --> 17:30.100
You don't know how good it feels to hold a million dollars.

17:30.100 --> 17:32.100
We're gonna have to tie her up, Phil.

17:32.100 --> 17:34.100
Get the rope. It's right behind you.

17:34.100 --> 18:03.100
Go on, Phil.

18:04.100 --> 18:24.100
You're a good girl, Daisy.

18:24.100 --> 18:26.100
Just keep quiet about it.

18:26.100 --> 18:29.100
Anybody asks you, you haven't seen anything, you understand?

18:29.100 --> 18:32.100
You've always been my favorite, Daisy.

18:32.100 --> 18:36.100
You can have a job with me as long as you want it.

18:36.100 --> 18:38.100
Just keep quiet about it.

18:38.100 --> 18:40.100
You don't know anything.

18:40.100 --> 18:42.100
Okay.

18:55.100 --> 18:58.100
Hey, Joe. I'll ask this fella here.

18:58.100 --> 19:00.100
Excuse me.

19:00.100 --> 19:04.100
You ain't seen a little red-headed girl about so high, have you?

19:04.100 --> 19:06.100
Why don't you look inside, buddy?

19:06.100 --> 19:08.100
Get a ticket right over there.

19:08.100 --> 19:10.100
Right this way, folks.

19:10.100 --> 19:12.100
Follow me.

19:12.100 --> 19:29.100
It ain't no use in asking him.

19:29.100 --> 19:32.100
He's got a gullet full of sword in him.

19:32.100 --> 19:34.100
He wouldn't tell you anything anyway.

19:34.100 --> 19:37.100
These corny people stick together tighter than those bartenders in San Francisco

19:37.100 --> 19:39.100
the time they tried to Shanghai our pop.

19:39.100 --> 19:41.100
How do we know she's even here?

19:41.100 --> 19:43.100
How do we know she's even here at all?

19:43.100 --> 19:45.100
Where else would she be?

19:45.100 --> 19:48.100
Salt Lake or St. Louis, for all we know.

19:48.100 --> 19:51.100
Boss, I think we can cover more ground if we split up.

19:51.100 --> 19:54.100
Why don't you and Harriet look out here? I'll check behind those tents.

19:54.100 --> 19:56.100
All right. You be careful, you hear?

19:56.100 --> 19:58.100
Right.

19:58.100 --> 20:01.100
Daddy, don't get mixed up in some of that dangerous women I ever saw.

20:01.100 --> 20:03.100
Now, you be careful what you say, Hoss.

20:03.100 --> 20:05.100
Jennifer's my best friend.

20:05.100 --> 20:07.100
Now, listen, if you said I ain't close to her,

20:07.100 --> 20:24.100
I'd be real friendly and come on back here.

20:24.100 --> 20:25.100
Yes? What is it?

20:25.100 --> 20:28.100
I saw your wagon. I was just trying to find out who's in charge of the show.

20:28.100 --> 20:30.100
I am. Why, do you have a complaint?

20:30.100 --> 20:32.100
No, no complaints.

20:32.100 --> 20:35.100
See, I came here with a girl tonight. Now she's disappeared.

20:35.100 --> 20:37.100
I wondered if you might have seen her.

20:37.100 --> 20:40.100
Sonny, I see an awful lot of people, and happily, all paying customers.

20:40.100 --> 20:42.100
Yeah, well, about this girl.

20:42.100 --> 20:44.100
Her name's Jennifer, Jennifer Beal.

20:44.100 --> 20:47.100
She's 18. She has light red hair, brown eyes.

20:47.100 --> 20:51.100
Well, from your description, I can understand why you feel badly about losing her.

20:51.100 --> 20:53.100
But you know what they say.

20:53.100 --> 20:56.100
They don't always go home with the fellas that brought them.

20:56.100 --> 21:24.100
Well, I can't help you.

21:24.100 --> 21:28.100
May I come in?

21:28.100 --> 21:32.100
My name is Joe Cartwright. I just wondered if...

21:32.100 --> 21:35.100
You're a little young for this sort of thing, aren't you, Joe Cartwright?

21:35.100 --> 21:38.100
Oh, look, you don't understand.

21:38.100 --> 21:40.100
You see, I didn't come here to...

21:40.100 --> 21:42.100
What I mean is...

21:42.100 --> 21:44.100
Exactly what do you mean, Joe?

21:44.100 --> 21:47.100
Well, I'm sorry I barged in on you like this, Miss Lilligia.

21:47.100 --> 21:48.100
Call me Della.

21:48.100 --> 21:51.100
Thanks, Della. See, I brought my girl to the show tonight.

21:51.100 --> 21:54.100
Yes, I remember seeing her. She's very pretty.

21:54.100 --> 21:57.100
Well, she's disappeared. I've been all over the carnival asking questions.

21:57.100 --> 21:59.100
Nobody seems to want to give me any answers.

21:59.100 --> 22:01.100
That's why when I saw your light, I...

22:01.100 --> 22:06.100
Sure.

22:06.100 --> 22:08.100
It hurts to lose someone, doesn't it?

22:08.100 --> 22:10.100
Well, it's not quite as painful as all that.

22:10.100 --> 22:13.100
It's just that I am supposed to make sure she's all right.

22:13.100 --> 22:16.100
I don't think she's run off with another fella.

22:16.100 --> 22:18.100
All right, tell me about her. Who is she?

22:18.100 --> 22:20.100
Her name's Jennifer Beal.

22:20.100 --> 22:22.100
Well, is there anything special about her?

22:22.100 --> 22:26.100
Or for some reason, someone might want to harm her?

22:26.100 --> 22:28.100
Yeah, there's one big one.

22:28.100 --> 22:31.100
Her father's one of the richest men on the comm staff.

22:31.100 --> 22:34.100
Yes, that is a reason.

22:34.100 --> 22:38.100
You stay here, Joe. I'll go ask some questions.

22:41.100 --> 22:44.100
Maybe I can find your girl for you.

22:44.100 --> 22:47.100
Thanks, Della.

22:47.100 --> 22:50.100
Della.

22:59.100 --> 23:01.100
What you doing here, boy?

23:01.100 --> 23:04.100
You looking for something to steal?

23:04.100 --> 23:07.100
Now, wait a minute, mister. I'm no thief.

23:07.100 --> 23:09.100
Well, I think you are.

23:09.100 --> 23:12.100
I think we better teach you a lesson.

23:12.100 --> 23:17.100
Now, look, wait a minute, fellas. We can talk...

23:34.100 --> 23:36.100
Well, good job, boys.

23:36.100 --> 23:39.100
Very good. That'll teach them from stupid round up.

23:39.100 --> 23:42.100
Wait a minute.

23:42.100 --> 23:44.100
Is this his gun?

23:44.100 --> 23:46.100
That's right.

23:46.100 --> 23:48.100
Good.

23:53.100 --> 23:55.100
Hello, Della. How'd you do?

23:55.100 --> 23:58.100
Pretty well. How did you do?

23:58.100 --> 24:00.100
What's that supposed to mean?

24:00.100 --> 24:02.100
Nothing on your mind?

24:02.100 --> 24:05.100
Well, a young man just paid me a visit in my tent,

24:05.100 --> 24:09.100
and it seems he lost his girlfriend.

24:09.100 --> 24:12.100
What's that got to do with me?

24:12.100 --> 24:15.100
Well, it just sounded familiar, that's all.

24:15.100 --> 24:17.100
Oh, honey.

24:17.100 --> 24:20.100
I thought we weren't going to have any more of those suspicions.

24:20.100 --> 24:23.100
I saw you talking to a girl earlier, Phil,

24:23.100 --> 24:25.100
and I saw you bring her in here.

24:25.100 --> 24:28.100
And if you'd hung around a few minutes, you would have seen her leave.

24:28.100 --> 24:30.100
Oh, she was a child.

24:30.100 --> 24:33.100
An innocent kid looking for adventure.

24:33.100 --> 24:36.100
I got rid of her fast.

24:36.100 --> 24:39.100
You are telling me the truth, aren't you?

24:39.100 --> 24:41.100
You're not lying to me.

24:41.100 --> 24:43.100
Oh, Della, there's nobody else but you.

24:43.100 --> 24:45.100
Can't you believe that?

24:45.100 --> 24:47.100
Sure. I can believe it.

24:47.100 --> 24:49.100
Well, then let's forget about the girl.

24:49.100 --> 24:52.100
I saw the kid who visited you in your tent.

24:52.100 --> 24:56.100
I told him maybe his girl saw a boy she liked better and went home with him.

24:56.100 --> 24:58.100
I guess that's what she did.

24:58.100 --> 25:00.100
Sure.

25:00.100 --> 25:02.100
Now, come on, you're tired.

25:02.100 --> 25:05.100
I'm just going to rest because we're pulling out tonight.

25:05.100 --> 25:07.100
Tonight? Why tonight?

25:07.100 --> 25:10.100
I thought we were going to play this stand for the rest of the week.

25:10.100 --> 25:12.100
We were. But I changed my mind.

25:12.100 --> 25:14.100
See you later.

25:14.100 --> 25:17.100
You have got the girl, haven't you, Phil?

25:17.100 --> 25:19.100
Are we going to start that all over again?

25:19.100 --> 25:21.100
Oh, stop lying to me.

25:21.100 --> 25:24.100
I know who she is and what you're trying to do.

25:24.100 --> 25:26.100
All right, so you know.

25:26.100 --> 25:29.100
Della, this is the biggest thing that ever happened to us.

25:29.100 --> 25:32.100
You think you can kidnap Joshua Beal's daughter and get away with it?

25:32.100 --> 25:34.100
She fell into our laps.

25:34.100 --> 25:36.100
I didn't invite her in here. She walked in.

25:36.100 --> 25:38.100
She's worth a million dollars to us.

25:38.100 --> 25:41.100
Do you know the kind of life we can have with a million dollars?

25:41.100 --> 25:44.100
Oh, Phil, I love you.

25:44.100 --> 25:46.100
I guess I always will.

25:46.100 --> 25:49.100
But I'd rather see you dead than mixed up in something like this.

25:49.100 --> 25:51.100
Della, we're not going to harm the girl.

25:51.100 --> 25:54.100
When Joshua Beal pays off, we'll turn her loose.

25:54.100 --> 25:56.100
How can you stand there and say you're going to turn her loose?

25:56.100 --> 25:58.100
Don't you know she'll remember you?

25:58.100 --> 26:00.100
If you go through with this, you can't turn her loose.

26:00.100 --> 26:02.100
Who said anything about turning her loose?

26:07.100 --> 26:08.100
Does she know where the girl is?

26:08.100 --> 26:10.100
No.

26:14.100 --> 26:16.100
You shouldn't have told Della about the girl, Phil.

26:16.100 --> 26:18.100
I didn't tell her. She figured it out.

26:18.100 --> 26:20.100
Well, that's too bad.

26:20.100 --> 26:22.100
Yes, that's very bad, isn't it, Phil?

26:22.100 --> 26:28.100
All right, it's too bad.

26:44.100 --> 26:46.100
I don't know where else we can look.

26:46.100 --> 26:49.100
We done covered every inch of this convo.

26:49.100 --> 26:52.100
We're going to have to go through twice.

26:52.100 --> 26:55.100
Yeah, I think I might as well be getting you home, Harriet.

26:55.100 --> 26:58.100
There ain't no use in your folks thinking you disappeared, too.

26:58.100 --> 27:00.100
Wonder what happened to little Joe?

27:00.100 --> 27:03.100
Hoss?

27:03.100 --> 27:05.100
Hey, Joe.

27:05.100 --> 27:07.100
What happened? What's the matter, boy?

27:07.100 --> 27:09.100
Four guys just piling up in there.

27:09.100 --> 27:11.100
I'll be all right, don't worry.

27:11.100 --> 27:13.100
What happened to your gun?

27:13.100 --> 27:16.100
They must have taken it after they beat me up.

27:16.100 --> 27:18.100
You know, there's something real wrong around here, Hoss.

27:18.100 --> 27:21.100
I think it's about because I was asking questions about Jennifer.

27:21.100 --> 27:23.100
You mean that this isn't just one of her jokes?

27:23.100 --> 27:25.100
You think something's happened to her?

27:25.100 --> 27:28.100
Hey, listen, Hoss, you take Harriet home on the way stop,

27:28.100 --> 27:30.100
I tell Sheriff Brady to get over here.

27:30.100 --> 27:32.100
The Colonel was quick as he can.

27:32.100 --> 27:34.100
What are you going to be doing in the meantime?

27:34.100 --> 27:36.100
The only thing I can do, keep on looking.

27:36.100 --> 27:38.100
Joe, you gotta find her.

27:38.100 --> 27:40.100
Yeah, Harriet, I know.

27:40.100 --> 27:42.100
I'll bring the sheriff myself. Be back in a minute.

27:42.100 --> 27:50.100
Joe.

27:50.100 --> 27:52.100
Joe, what happened to you? Where were you?

27:52.100 --> 27:55.100
Oh, honey, that's a fine question for you to ask me.

27:55.100 --> 27:57.100
I've had your four friends work me over.

27:57.100 --> 28:00.100
Work you over? Joe, I didn't.

28:00.100 --> 28:02.100
I've got to talk to you.

28:02.100 --> 28:09.100
It's about Jennifer.

28:09.100 --> 28:11.100
All right, you said you knew something about Jennifer.

28:11.100 --> 28:13.100
Please believe me, Joe, I'm trying to help you find your girl.

28:13.100 --> 28:15.100
She's somewhere here in the carnival.

28:15.100 --> 28:18.100
Oh, we're going to find her all right. I've already sent for the sheriff.

28:18.100 --> 28:22.100
Please, Joe, let me do this my way. Don't call in the sheriff.

28:22.100 --> 28:24.100
The carnival people are good friends of mine. They'll help.

28:24.100 --> 28:26.100
I've already seen the way they help. I'll take the sheriff.

28:26.100 --> 28:30.100
But if the sheriff comes, then a lot of innocent people will be hurt.

28:30.100 --> 28:33.100
People I love and that are good people that know nothing about this.

28:33.100 --> 28:35.100
I'm sorry. I can't help that.

28:35.100 --> 28:36.100
Joe, let me...

28:36.100 --> 28:53.100
No!

28:53.100 --> 28:56.100
You killed her!

28:56.100 --> 28:59.100
No, no, actually, no!

28:59.100 --> 29:06.100
Della wouldn't want it that way.

29:06.100 --> 29:09.100
Come on. Come on, Hercules.

29:09.100 --> 29:11.100
Come on. I'm going to kill you.

29:11.100 --> 29:13.100
No!

29:13.100 --> 29:14.100
What happened?

29:14.100 --> 29:20.100
Come on, Thor.

29:20.100 --> 29:22.100
Where is the new sheriff? Where? What happened?

29:22.100 --> 29:25.100
All right, quiet! Quiet down, all of you!

29:25.100 --> 29:27.100
I'm in charge here.

29:27.100 --> 29:30.100
There's a lot of things I gotta know.

29:30.100 --> 29:32.100
Well, first of all, I didn't do it.

29:32.100 --> 29:34.100
Second, they got Jennifer hit out around here someplace.

29:34.100 --> 29:36.100
You better forget about Jennifer. There's been a murder here.

29:36.100 --> 29:40.100
Yeah, I know. That girl was killed because she was trying to help me find Jennifer.

29:40.100 --> 29:42.100
You know anything about this, Reed?

29:42.100 --> 29:44.100
Well, boy, talk to me. I've questioned everybody in this show,

29:44.100 --> 29:47.100
and nobody knows anything about her.

29:47.100 --> 29:49.100
Is this your gun?

29:49.100 --> 29:51.100
Yes, it's my gun, but I didn't have it when this girl...

29:51.100 --> 29:53.100
I think you better come along with me.

29:53.100 --> 29:55.100
Look, I'm not going to leave. Here, we'll find Jennifer.

29:55.100 --> 29:58.100
Son, I know Jennifer as well as you do. Maybe better.

29:58.100 --> 30:03.100
I had a posse out combing the hills for her that time she ran off to San Francisco.

30:03.100 --> 30:06.100
Joe, maybe you ought not to make any more trouble for yourself.

30:06.100 --> 30:08.100
Come along.

30:08.100 --> 30:10.100
Hey, look what happened.

30:10.100 --> 30:12.100
Hey, you calling this?

30:12.100 --> 30:18.100
Cartman, in here. I'm trying to help you.

30:18.100 --> 30:20.100
In here.

30:20.100 --> 30:28.100
I don't know what you're up to, mister, but thanks a lot.

30:28.100 --> 30:33.100
I'm not up to anything. I'm Roudin. I was Della Thompson's closest friend.

30:33.100 --> 30:35.100
I don't believe you killed her.

30:35.100 --> 30:39.100
Ma'am, are you sure you didn't see him come by here?

30:39.100 --> 30:43.100
I didn't see anything. I just sit here. I don't see nothing.

30:43.100 --> 30:48.100
Sheriff, I know little Joe didn't kill that woman,

30:48.100 --> 30:52.100
but I'd rather see him in your jail than running loose around here.

30:52.100 --> 30:54.100
We're not going to learn anything here.

30:54.100 --> 30:58.100
Now, listen to me. There's only so many wagons and so many tents,

30:58.100 --> 31:00.100
so we'll search them one by one.

31:00.100 --> 31:03.100
Boss, you take one party. I'll take the other.

31:03.100 --> 31:05.100
Right.

31:12.100 --> 31:14.100
It could be kidnapping.

31:14.100 --> 31:16.100
I'm sure Della thought so too.

31:16.100 --> 31:20.100
She was just getting ready to tell me something when she was killed.

31:20.100 --> 31:25.100
I believe you, Joe, but I don't know what to do about it.

31:25.100 --> 31:27.100
What can you do?

31:27.100 --> 31:29.100
Well, we're a funny bunch here.

31:29.100 --> 31:33.100
In time, we get to believing our own acts.

31:33.100 --> 31:37.100
Maybe I can do a little mind reading.

31:37.100 --> 31:42.100
Come on.

31:42.100 --> 31:45.100
In here.

32:01.100 --> 32:04.100
There's no use searching for the girl in here, Hercules.

32:04.100 --> 32:07.100
I'm looking for the man who killed Della.

32:07.100 --> 32:10.100
Do you think I'd protect anyone that harmed Della?

32:10.100 --> 32:14.100
I gotta find him. I gotta kill him with my bare hands.

32:14.100 --> 32:18.100
We stole Della. I'd kill anybody that harmed her.

32:23.100 --> 32:26.100
I'm your friend, Hercules. Don't you trust me?

32:26.100 --> 32:34.100
I trust you because Della is dead.

32:34.100 --> 32:49.100
You stay here. I'm going out back.

32:49.100 --> 32:59.100
You stay here.

33:14.100 --> 33:16.100
You there, Rodin?

33:16.100 --> 33:20.100
Yes, I'm here. I told you there was no trick.

33:20.100 --> 33:24.100
I'll find him, and when I do, I'll kill him.

33:24.100 --> 33:32.100
I wish there was some way to convince him you were innocent.

33:32.100 --> 33:34.100
Yes, but why?

33:34.100 --> 33:37.100
You'd make a good ally.

33:37.100 --> 33:41.100
He's really a nice man, and he was in love with Della Thompson.

33:41.100 --> 33:43.100
Him?

33:43.100 --> 33:48.100
Well, we're all freaks here, one way or another.

33:48.100 --> 33:51.100
Doesn't mean we don't have any heart.

33:51.100 --> 33:53.100
Thanks.

33:53.100 --> 33:57.100
What are you going to do?

33:57.100 --> 33:59.100
Keep on searching.

33:59.100 --> 34:03.100
I know these folks are friends of yours, but one of them's a killer.

34:03.100 --> 34:13.100
I got to get to Jennifer before he does.

34:23.100 --> 34:25.100
Don't make a sound.

34:25.100 --> 34:31.100
I'm sorry.

34:31.100 --> 34:35.100
You're a forceful one, aren't you?

34:39.100 --> 34:43.100
I'm terribly sorry about that, sir.

34:43.100 --> 34:45.100
I thought you were going to scream.

34:45.100 --> 34:48.100
Just because a handsome man came in my tent?

34:48.100 --> 34:51.100
Why, what makes you think I'd scream?

34:51.100 --> 34:54.100
You're the one they're looking for, aren't you?

34:54.100 --> 34:56.100
They're looking for me all over the place.

34:56.100 --> 34:59.100
I think I better get out of here before I get you in a lot of trouble.

34:59.100 --> 35:01.100
Don't go.

35:01.100 --> 35:04.100
Maybe I'd like to get into a lot of trouble.

35:04.100 --> 35:08.100
Well, ma'am, maybe sometime we could talk.

35:08.100 --> 35:10.100
That's what they all say.

35:10.100 --> 35:13.100
Now, why don't you just relax and we can get acquainted?

35:13.100 --> 35:17.100
Well, ma'am, I just really don't think this is a time to get acquainted.

35:17.100 --> 35:21.100
I saw you earlier this evening with that girl.

35:21.100 --> 35:23.100
Now, I thought she was too young for you.

35:23.100 --> 35:27.100
I think you'd prefer a more sophisticated lady like me.

35:27.100 --> 35:29.100
Now, wouldn't you?

35:29.100 --> 35:30.100
Ma'am, I...

35:30.100 --> 35:32.100
Can I come in, ma'am?

35:32.100 --> 35:35.100
Quick, behind the dresses.

35:35.100 --> 35:36.100
I'll protect you.

35:36.100 --> 35:40.100
And, uh, after they've gone...

35:43.100 --> 35:45.100
Uh, you seen a young fellow go by here?

35:45.100 --> 35:46.100
Doesn't belong to the carnival?

35:46.100 --> 35:48.100
No, I haven't seen anyone.

35:48.100 --> 35:50.100
Ma'am?

35:50.100 --> 35:53.100
They're gone, honey.

35:53.100 --> 36:20.100
Honey?

36:23.100 --> 36:25.100
Say, has anybody searched this wagon yet?

36:25.100 --> 36:28.100
I'm sure the other party searched it thoroughly.

36:28.100 --> 36:30.100
They've searched here, Daisy, haven't they?

36:30.100 --> 36:32.100
Yes, they've searched very good.

36:32.100 --> 36:34.100
Well, I didn't see it. I think I'll take a look.

36:34.100 --> 36:38.100
Sheriff, if you don't mind, there are very few people that Daisy lets into her wagon.

36:38.100 --> 36:42.100
I'd rather somebody search it that she knows. You understand?

36:42.100 --> 36:44.100
Yeah, I think I understand.

36:44.100 --> 36:47.100
Gurnard, why don't you take a look and satisfy the sheriff?

36:47.100 --> 36:57.100
Well, if that's what the sheriff wants.

36:57.100 --> 37:13.100
Look in there behind those clothes.

37:13.100 --> 37:27.100
Gurnard, look in the back of the wagon.

37:27.100 --> 37:56.100
Nobody here, sheriff.

37:56.100 --> 38:24.100
Any luck at all?

38:24.100 --> 38:26.100
Nope.

38:26.100 --> 38:29.100
Looks like that little brother of mine disappeared as completely as that gal did.

38:29.100 --> 38:31.100
Now, sheriff, are you convinced she's not here?

38:31.100 --> 38:33.100
I'll decide that.

38:33.100 --> 38:34.100
As you wish.

38:34.100 --> 38:36.100
Just trying to cooperate.

38:36.100 --> 38:38.100
Sheriff, we gotta start tearing down camp.

38:38.100 --> 38:41.100
We open in Placerville the day after tomorrow.

38:41.100 --> 38:42.100
Isn't that right, Mr. Reed?

38:42.100 --> 38:43.100
Mm-hmm.

38:43.100 --> 38:44.100
We're gonna find the guy that killed Della.

38:44.100 --> 38:46.100
There's coffee up in the cook tent.

38:46.100 --> 38:48.100
Why don't we all settle down for a bit?

38:48.100 --> 38:49.100
It's a good idea, Mr. Rodin.

38:49.100 --> 38:55.100
Right this way, sheriff.

38:55.100 --> 38:58.100
I'd like to talk to you.

38:58.100 --> 38:59.100
What about?

38:59.100 --> 39:01.100
I think you know.

39:01.100 --> 39:04.100
I'm no more of a mind reader than you are.

39:04.100 --> 39:07.100
No, but you are a carnival man.

39:07.100 --> 39:10.100
A lot of people depend on you, Phil.

39:10.100 --> 39:12.100
Well, haven't I always come through for them?

39:12.100 --> 39:13.100
Yes.

39:13.100 --> 39:18.100
But will you come through for them now?

39:18.100 --> 39:21.100
You think I had something to do with that girl's disappearance, don't you?

39:21.100 --> 39:26.100
I think you could shed some light on it, yes.

39:26.100 --> 39:30.100
Well, you're wrong.

39:30.100 --> 39:33.100
If I am, I'll back you up.

39:33.100 --> 39:42.100
But if I'm right, I'll turn your people against you, Phil, and I can do it.

39:42.100 --> 39:46.100
Hercules, for one, has always hated you for the way you treated Della.

39:46.100 --> 40:03.100
Hey, thanks for not sneaking up on me.

40:03.100 --> 40:04.100
You little galoot.

40:04.100 --> 40:05.100
What are you trying to do?

40:05.100 --> 40:07.100
I'm still trying to find Jennifer.

40:07.100 --> 40:09.100
She's around here someplace, Hoss.

40:09.100 --> 40:10.100
Della knew it.

40:10.100 --> 40:12.100
That's what she was trying to tell me when she was killed.

40:12.100 --> 40:14.100
Now, let's go over it again.

40:14.100 --> 40:16.100
Just how much was she able to tell you?

40:16.100 --> 40:18.100
Nothing.

40:18.100 --> 40:21.100
Though she wanted me to know, and yet she didn't want me to know.

40:21.100 --> 40:22.100
I don't know.

40:22.100 --> 40:24.100
Maybe she was trying to protect someone.

40:24.100 --> 40:26.100
Of course.

40:26.100 --> 40:28.100
I should have known.

40:28.100 --> 40:29.100
Phil Reed.

40:29.100 --> 40:31.100
She would want to protect him.

40:31.100 --> 40:34.100
Mr. Rudine, if Phil Reed knows something about this,

40:34.100 --> 40:36.100
then he ain't telling how it should get out of him.

40:36.100 --> 40:39.100
Then you'd have the Carnival people and the sheriff down on you.

40:39.100 --> 40:41.100
I know these people.

40:41.100 --> 40:44.100
They've got a strange kind of loyalty.

40:44.100 --> 40:45.100
Yeah, I can believe that.

40:45.100 --> 40:48.100
I couldn't find out a thing from any of them.

40:48.100 --> 40:52.100
Hercules is the only one that Mike turned against Reed.

40:52.100 --> 40:56.100
You got any idea how you can convince him to help us?

40:56.100 --> 40:59.100
Not so long as he's with the others.

40:59.100 --> 41:00.100
Yeah, I suppose we could get him away.

41:00.100 --> 41:02.100
Someplace where we could talk to him.

41:02.100 --> 41:04.100
Yeah, but how you figuring on doing that?

